From 2c3e7b4012158814d4be8fa6ba7b694e2eab0244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:45:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: write JSON members onto bind-mounted and symlinked files

A ~/.claude.json persisted by impermanence is either a single-file bind
mount or a symlink into the persistent store. Renaming the staged temp
onto a mount point fails EBUSY (EXDEV across mounts), so every sync
failed with "failed to write ~/.claude.json"; renaming it over a symlink
replaces the link with a plain file, silently dropping persistence.

Keep the rename as the first choice. When it fails EBUSY or EXDEV, write
the staged bytes into the destination in place (same inode and mode),
as Claude Code itself does, and remove the temp. Member writes follow a
symlink first, so the temp is staged beside the real file and the link
survives; a link into an unwritable directory is replaced as before.
---
